1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,350
A task is a promise.

2
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:03,550
You promise points.

3
00:00:03,550 --> 00:00:05,150
The game promises drops.

4
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:07,550
Only one of you is lying.

5
00:00:13,150 --> 00:00:16,350
Tasks live in your event's manager, under Tasks.

6
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:19,550
Click New task and you get this form.

7
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:21,550
It looks like a lot.

8
00:00:21,550 --> 00:00:23,150
It is a lot.

9
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:26,350
But it's the good kind of a lot.

10
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:28,350
First, the type.

11
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:31,550
Items, kill count, XP, skill levels, personal bests,

12
00:00:31,550 --> 00:00:34,750
pets, combat achievements, slayer tasks, total loot value.

13
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:38,750
Nearly all of them are scored automatically from the plugin.

14
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:43,150
The ones that aren't, like custom tasks, wait for an admin.

15
00:00:43,950 --> 00:00:45,550
Item tasks have modes.

16
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:46,750
One specific item.

17
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:48,750
Any items from a list.

18
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:53,950
Different items, so the fifth Bandos tasset in a row doesn't count five

19
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:54,350
times.

20
00:00:54,350 --> 00:00:55,950
All of a list.

21
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:57,150
Points per item.

22
00:00:57,150 --> 00:01:00,750
Combined requirements, like every godsword shard plus any hilt.

23
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:04,350
Or either-or: a boss pet, or five thousand kills.

24
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:05,550
Whichever comes first.

25
00:01:05,550 --> 00:01:07,550
It won't be the pet.

26
00:01:08,350 --> 00:01:12,350
Search for the item, drop it in, set the points.

27
00:01:12,350 --> 00:01:15,550
Fifty points for a twisted bow feels fair.

28
00:01:15,550 --> 00:01:17,150
It is not fair.

29
00:01:17,150 --> 00:01:19,950
Nothing about a twisted bow is fair.

30
00:01:20,750 --> 00:01:22,350
Every task explains itself.

31
00:01:22,350 --> 00:01:26,750
Open What counts and it tells you exactly what gets credited.

32
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:31,950
And it's been stress-tested by clan members, who are the most creative people

33
00:01:31,950 --> 00:01:33,950
alive when points are involved.

34
00:01:34,750 --> 00:01:39,550
Kill count from the plugin and from Wise Old Man is merged,

35
00:01:39,550 --> 00:01:42,350
never added, so no kill counts twice.

36
00:01:42,350 --> 00:01:45,950
A drop and its collection log entry count once.

37
00:01:45,950 --> 00:01:49,150
Slayer tasks skip Turael and Spria by default,

38
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:51,950
so Turael skipping will not save you.

39
00:01:51,950 --> 00:01:55,150
And only things you do after joining count.

40
00:01:55,150 --> 00:01:56,350
Yes, we checked.

41
00:01:57,150 --> 00:01:59,550
Want a human in the loop?

42
00:01:59,550 --> 00:02:03,550
Tick review on a task, or on the whole event,

43
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:06,750
and completions land here, in the review queue.

44
00:02:06,750 --> 00:02:09,550
Confirm, reject, or hand out points manually.

45
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:14,750
Loot value tasks can auto-accept small drops, because nobody should have to approve

46
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:15,950
three hundred bones.

47
00:02:16,750 --> 00:02:20,750
Every task you make is saved to a reusable library,

48
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:24,350
and there are a few hundred public presets already.

49
00:02:24,350 --> 00:02:28,350
Or press Fill for me, answer a couple of questions,

50
00:02:28,350 --> 00:02:31,550
and get a balanced list you can lock,

51
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:33,950
reroll, and pretend you wrote yourself.

52
00:02:34,750 --> 00:02:35,550
That's tasks.

53
00:02:35,550 --> 00:02:36,750
Next episode: points.

54
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:41,950
Who gets them, how bingo lines work, and why the person who went

55
00:02:41,950 --> 00:02:44,750
AFK on the winning team gets nothing.
